{"schema_version":"benchmark-q1-semantic-issue-coverage-judgment-luna5","question_id":"Q1-semantic-issue-coverage","status":"ok","judge_run_name":"luna8-v4-medium-196-glm-5.3-max-full200-2026-10-01","prediction_set_name":"glm-5.3-max-full200-2026-10-01","paper_id":"2409.01211","judge_input_sha256":"81c51591a95b5bfcdb590f155e3668089da9cd8f69a50c12cbc3f116699ad73c","gold_decisions":[{"gold_issue_id":"2409.01211:I001","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-004","focus_relation":"different_causal_subject","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2409.01211:I001:U001","2409.01211:I001:U002","2409.01211:I001:U003"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-004:U001","ISSUE-004:U005"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue concerns a false global classification of complete constant-curvature manifolds and the missing simple-connectedness hypothesis. ISSUE-004 concerns a false discretization/projection estimate caused by inadequate norms near the boundary; it does not diagnose the geometric classification defect.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2409.01211:I002","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-003","focus_relation":"different_operation_step_or_formula","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2409.01211:I002:U001","2409.01211:I002:U002","2409.01211:I002:U003"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-003:U001","ISSUE-003:U002","ISSUE-003:U007"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue is an unsupported uniform spatial consistency estimate at t=0 for unqualified data, requiring fourth-derivative regularity and domain qualification. ISSUE-003 identifies incorrect time-Taylor remainder kernels and prefactors in a time-discretization proof, which is a different formula and obligation.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2409.01211:I004","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-002","focus_relation":"different_operation_step_or_formula","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2409.01211:I004:U001","2409.01211:I004:U002","2409.01211:I004:U003","2409.01211:I004:U004"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-002:U001","ISSUE-002:U003","ISSUE-002:U008"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue is the unjustified use of a radius lemma restricted to D>2 when proving an all-h bound, requiring a separate D<=2 case. ISSUE-002 concerns a different boundary-row/stencil defect in a bounded-domain consistency estimate; it does not identify the missing case split or the invalid radius-lemma invocation in the tail-control proof.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[] }],"audit":{"all_gold_ids_decided":true,"all_ranked_candidates_considered":true,"target_type_not_used_for_identity":true,"severity_not_used_for_identity":true,"prediction_reuse_requires_explicit_issue_support":true,"each_gold_credited_at_most_once":true,"combined_entries_are_self_contained_diagnoses":true,"support_limit_three_respected":true}}